    \subfloat{\includegraphics[width=1\textwidth]{figures/bandwidth+comparison.pdf}}

    \caption{Bandwidth and memory type comparison. a) Spectral overlap of memory bandwidth and signal spectrum. For practical applications both signal wavelength and signal linewidth have to match the spectral properties of the memory. b) A memory in $\Lambda$-type configuration operates between ground- and storage states within one hyperfine manifold. c) Ladder-type memory configurations connect ground and storage state via full orbital transitions.}
