\subsection{Informative Seed Instructions Selection}

The initial data distribution largely determines the effectiveness of subsequent data synthesing, thus selecting a set of informative seed instructions is crucial for synthesizing high-quality instruction data.
Given the abundance of existing instruction datasets, aimlessly synthesizing existing data is of limited value. 
In contrast, it is more meaningful to focus on instructions that are currently underrepresented in existing datasets (expanding coverage), or those that are relatively difficult and expose model limitations in reasoning or knowledge (enhancing depth).
As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:data_selection}, we design four criteria to select informative instructions:

% 1. 高遵循难度：微调后的token-level agerage Cross Entropy Loss下降比例最小的50k条指令， 以保证指令集的难度

% 2. 长尾指令：将所有包含任意一个频率小于200的细粒度标签的低频知识或能力的指令收入种子指令集；随机采样30\%带有频率在[200, 500]内的指令到种子数据集内。以保证指令集的覆盖度。

% 3. 需要多种能力的指令：将所有细粒度标签数大于4个的指令包含在种子指令集内。直观上看，这样的指令需要更加综合的能力与知识，因此具有更大的深度。

% 4. 对于Base模型高loss的指令：这样的指令base模型可能较少被训练过，或者具有较高的难度，因而具有较高的loss。我们选取了$loss > mean(loss) + 1.96 * std(loss)$200k条指令加入种子数据集。

% 通过依次执行上述4个标准，我们从指令数据池中选择出了1.2M条种子指令。在上述过程中，我们采用llama-2-7B-base计算指令的loss，随后从指令集的每个大类中，均匀采样1000条，构成了一个子集，用以微调llama-2-7B-base模型，以计算token-level agerage Cross Entropy Loss的下降比例。

% Table~\ref{tab:dataset_summary}展示了种子数据集的来源，和筛选后的数量。基于上述步骤，我们合成了条指令数据。

\textbf{1. Hard-to-Follow Instructions}:
We select the 50k instructions with the smallest reduction in token-level average cross-entropy loss after fine-tuning, ensuring the retained instructions are challenging to follow.

\textbf{2. Long-Tail Instructions}:
To guarantee coverage, we include instructions that contain at least one fine-grained tag with a frequency below 200 in the seed set. Additionally, we randomly sample 30\% of the instructions that contain tags with frequencies in the range [200, 500].

\textbf{3. Multi-Skill Required Complex Instructions}:
Instructions associated with more than four fine-grained tags are included, as such instructions require more comprehensive reasoning or knowledge.

\textbf{4. Undertrained Instructions}:

These are instructions for which the base model performs poorly with a high loss value. This may either due to either a lack of exposure or inherent difficulty. We include 200k instructions with loss greater than $\text{mean(loss)} + 1.96 \times \text{std(loss)}$.

In particular, we use Llama-2-7B-base \citep{touvron2023llama} to compute the loss values for instructions.
To estimate the reduction ratio in token-level average cross-entropy loss, we fine-tune Llama-2-7B-base on a balanced instruction subset with 1,000 instructions per domain category.
Table~\ref{tab:dataset_summary} presents the sources of the seed data and the number of instructions retained after filtering.
By applying the above criteria sequentially, we select approximately 1.2 million informative instructions from the overall data pool.



