\subsection{Data Leakage Prevention}

Overlap between training and evaluation data can cause models to achieve inflated scores on familiar samples, leading to overestimated performance. We observe that many public instruction datasets include questions from common benchmarks like MT-Bench \citep{zheng2023judging} and AlpacaEval \citep{li2023alpacaeval}, which risks misleading evaluation.
To address this issue, we use the BGE model to compute semantic similarity between evaluation queries and instructions in the training data. This process involves multi-dimensional comparisons, including semantic understanding and structural features, to ensure accurate and comprehensive matching. Based on the similarity scores, we filter out overlapping entries, effectively preventing data leakage and preserving the reliability of model evaluation.

After the above procedures, we obtain 146,9391 new instruction samples.


