Previous studies distinguished regimes by the inspection of the aggregated coherence level of the network. For instance, in \cite{RING_CALIM}, the coherent state classification is based on the comparison of the SI parameter \cite{SI_DM_GOPAL} with a system of thresholds. By contrast, our approach performs a multi-aspect qualitative analysis of each instantaneous network state along three independent criteria: global coherence characteristic (fully coherent, chimera, or fully incoherent), number of coherent clusters, and type of intra-cluster coherence (synphase synchrony or traveling wave). Based on these three descriptors, we propose a classification of the states of the ring network in Table 1. 



