 We consider this strategy as a preliminary introduction to a potential further analysis. We acknowledge inherent simplifications, such as survival bias and omission of transaction costs. More advanced models, such as CAPM or Black-Litterman; see \cite{ sharpe1964capm,black1992}, account for market conditions and expert opinions, providing deeper insights. Furthermore, our approach primarily clusters data in space; a robust system should also diagnose crisis environments and adapt its decisions accordingly. However, our analysis suggests that the 20/60/20 rule may have promising applications in portfolio optimization, paving the way for future developments in this field.


