\section{Discussion}

In this paper, we have provided a new competitive line-graph-based method to detect an optimal routing path for trading in a DEX, like Uniswap V2, after testing against the DFS method. But how is its performance in running costs? As shown in Fig. \ref{running_cost}, its average running time almost increases exponentially, which may limit its application in large graphs. However, it is still very fast. For example, for a graph with 100 tokens, the average running time is about 0.1s. While the time is around 1.5s if we use the convex optimization method. 
