In recent years, manifold-based methods have gained attention in transfer learning, leveraging low-dimensional structures in high-dimensional data to improve alignment across domains without shared features or labels. For example, \cite{baktashmotlagh2014domain} assumes that the source and target domain distributions lie on a statistical manifold with Fisher-Rao geometry, and proposes to use Hellinger distance to perform domain alignment through sample selection and subspace projection, thereby improving traditional MMD-based methods. 
