    By definition, subsequent iterations of the doubling construction behave analogously to the first and so the formula in \cref{claim:one_step_crossings} also holds if all mentions of $P_0$ and $P_1$ are replaced by $P_i$ and $P_{i+1}$ and in particular $P_{t-1}$ and $P_t$, yielding a formula for $\crk(P_t; \col_t)$.
