\includegraphics
{xef4_example.png}\caption{Schematic depiction of how two degenerate and orthogonal molecular vibrational normal modes (left) can be superimposed with a $\pi/2$ phase difference in order to produce a circular polarization (right). Shown are the stretching modes of xenon tetrafluoride (XeF$_4$), with the teal and blue circles depicting the Xe and F atoms, respectively, and with grey lines depicting bonds. The red lines represent the atomic path while the red arrows indicate the relative direction of movement.}
\label{fig:def}
